From 05892892d0a2f99f3a23fd0ac72b806a6d788ddb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Kent <43362477+kentstephen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 21:16:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] manifest_store: put file access behind
 SourceFile/SourceOpener and test the error paths

The read loop, handle pooling, range clamping and every error message now
run against an in-memory opener in unit tests (short reads, failed seek,
failed read, EOF mid-read, missing file, pool cap, manifest open errors).
The unsafe DuckDB code shrinks to DuckDbFile and DuckDbOpener, which only
map FFI status codes.

Chunk decode errors in the scan now name the array and chunk indices.

New kerchunk_errors fixtures (missing file, range past EOF, offset beyond
EOF, truncated chunk) run the same paths through DuckDB's real filesystem
in the SQL suite.
